## SELF-TEST AFTER THE FIX (all arms held; the new ones are the seed + damage rules)
$ node scripts/mpd-tui-panels.ts --self-test
  ok   (a) an ABSENT leaf is seeded from the host's own default, so every builtin survives
  ok   (a) NEGATIVE CONTROL: a SEEDLESS absent leaf drops the builtins — the hazard the seed removes
  ok   (a) DAMAGE: a leaf naming NONE of the builtins is seeded with the whole default, ours preserved
  ok   (a) the damaged leaf's repair survives the merge as the full list
  ok   (a) CONTROL: a PARTIAL builtin selection is a position and is left byte-for-byte
  ok   (a) CONTROL: with no readable host default an ABSENT leaf REFUSES rather than seeding empty
  ok   (a) an EXISTING leaf is still usable when the host default cannot be read
[mpd-tui-panels] SELF-TEST PASS (all arms held)

